<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Narva (1700)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1700">1700</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narva">Narva</a> was fought in 1700 at the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>, when about 8,000 Swedish troops under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII</a> routed a much larger Russian army besieging Narva. It was one of the finest tactical victories of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>. For the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> the defeat prompted Peter I's military reforms, which created a standing professional army on the Western European model.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-narva-1700.jpg" alt="Battle of Narva (1700)" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gustaf Cederström · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narva_(Gustaf_Cederstr%C3%B6m)_-_Nationalmuseum_-_18638.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
